        {
          "id": 823777546,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "```\nwireshark$ ls -l wireshark-qt*\n-rwxrwxrwx 1 root root      8 Apr 29  2021 wireshark-qt.cflags\n-rwxrwxrwx 1 root root     88 Apr 29  2021 wireshark-qt.config\n-rwxrwxrwx 1 root root     11 Apr 29  2021 wireshark-qt.creator\n-rwxrwxrwx 1 root root  14448 Jul 21  2021 wireshark-qt.creator.user\n-rwxrwxrwx 1 root root  23547 Apr 30  2021 wireshark-qt.creator.user.479b36c\n-rwxrwxrwx 1 root root     10 Apr 29  2021 wireshark-qt.cxxflags\n-rwxrwxrwx 1 root root 118096 Apr 29  2021 wireshark-qt.files\n-rwxrwxrwx 1 root root   3576 Apr 29  2021 wireshark-qt.includes\nwireshark$\n```\n  \nWhich matches up with when Creator was installed/tested:  \n```\nqtcreator-4.14.2$ ls -l Inst*\n-rwxrwxrwx 1 root root 11407 Apr 29  2021 InstallationLog.txt\n\n************************************* Invoked: Thu Apr 29 14:05:37 2021\n[0] Arguments: C:\\Users\\IEUser\\Downloads\\qt-creator-opensource-windows-x86_64-4.14.2.exe\n```\n  \nI can't find it now but probably came across a document that mentioned building a `wireshark-qt` project in Creator.",
          "author": {
